<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://schema.org/creativeWorkStatus> "stable" .
<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://schema.org/description> "The sanctioned computation of WAU for a trailing 7-day window ending on a given day." .
<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://schema.org/expires> "2026-12-31T00:00:00+00:00"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://schema.org/isBasedOn> <https://acme.example/knowledge/metric-defs-rfc> .
<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://schema.org/keywords> "engagement" .
<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://schema.org/keywords> "growth" .
<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://schema.org/name> "Weekly Active Users count" .
<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://schema.org/runtimePlatform> "bigquery" .
<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://schema.org/text> "# Computation\n\n    SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT user_id) AS wau\n    FROM `acme.events.user_events`\n    WHERE event_name IN UNNEST(@qualifying_events)\n      AND DATE(event_ts) BETWEEN DATE_SUB(@week_end, INTERVAL 6 DAY) AND @week_end\n\nThe computation binds only the declared parameters; qualifying events are\nfixed by the metric definitions RFC.[^metric-defs-rfc] Backs the\n[Weekly Active Users](/metrics/weekly-active-users.md) metric.\n\n[^metric-defs-rfc]: Metric definitions RFC" .
<https://acme.example/knowledge/computations/weekly-active-users-count> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/lokf/AttestedComputation> .
